":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nIssue is consistent across versions:\n4.5.1-stable\n4.6-stable\n4.7_dev5\n4.7_dev4\n\nIssue does not occur in 4.4.1-stable.\n\n\n### System information\n\nVulkan, NVIDIA RTX3070, Forward Clustered, Windows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nFound this issue while investigating https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118930:\n\nWhen baking a lightmap with the sky enabled, the engine crashes with the following message:\n```\n[url]drivers\\vulkan\\rendering_context_driver_vulkan.cpp:646[/url] - VALIDATION - Message Id Number: 20145586 | Message Id Name: Undefined-Value-StorageImage-FormatMismatch-ImageView\n\tvkCmdDispatch(): the storage image descriptor [lb]VkDescriptorSet 0x53200000005320[lb]RID:664921066963593], Set 0, Binding 0, Index 0] is accessed by a OpTypeImage that has a Format operand Rgba8 (equivalent to VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM) which doesn't match the VkImageView 0x52e700000052e7[lb]RenderBuffer rb_ssao/final View] format (VK_FORMAT_R8_UNORM). Any loads or stores with the variable will produce undefined values to the whole image (not just the texel being accessed).\nSpec information at https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/textures.html#textures-format-validation\n\tObjects - 3\n\t\tObject[lb]0] - VK_OBJECT_TYPE_PIPELINE, Handle 1028043371971495, Name \"RID:2044404432963\"\n\t\tObject[lb]1] - VK_OBJECT_TYPE_DESCRIPTOR_SET, Handle 23397607439094560, Name \"RID:664921066963593\"\n\t\tObject[lb]2] - VK_OBJECT_TYPE_IMAGE_VIEW, Handle 23334935276311271, Name \"RenderBuffer rb_ssao/final View\"\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Run engine with `<godot_version>.exe --gpu-validation --rendering-driver vulkan`\n- Add a mesh with UV2 (e.g. new MeshInstance and cube mesh, enable UV2) and a lightmap and bake it\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":